real finding: Kafka message CreateTime (1789227251335ms = 15:34:11.335) exactly matches
the Postgres outbox createdat (15:34:11.33558) because our connector config maps
'transforms.outbox.table.field.event.timestamp: createdat' - the EventRouter uses the
DB row's own timestamp as the Kafka record timestamp, not real publish wall-clock time.
This is real, correct Debezium behavior (useful for preserving business event time), but
means Kafka's own timestamp cannot measure relay lag here. Using the consumer's real
processing log timestamp instead, which genuinely reflects when the message was actually
receivable end-to-end (including the injected 3s latency).
